WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:05.650
It was the summer of 2012 in Damascus, and
for the people of Syria, it certainly seemed

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.400
like all the predictions about “The End
of the World” were coming true.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:15.900
The Syrian civil war was raging between multiple
rebel groups and the dictator Bashar Al-Assad,

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.740
whose government was shelling its own people,
as well as using chemical weapons and brutal

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.880
campaigns of violence across the country in
hopes of quelling the rebellion.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:31.630
Little did they know, amidst all this pain
and bloodshed, something even more dangerous

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.840
was brewing.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:38.229
An anomalous phenomenon in the sunny plains
North of Damascus that may pose a threat to

00:00:38.229 --> 00:00:39.780
all of humanity someday.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:46.059
A threat known to the SCP Foundation as SCP-3989…

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:48.019
The Bone Orchard.

00:00:48.019 --> 00:00:53.829
This temporal and spatial anomaly was discovered
a few years earlier in 2009, before the Syrian

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:56.300
civil war even officially began.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.549
It’s strange for a highly dangerous Keter
Class anomaly to be discovered under such

00:01:00.549 --> 00:01:03.260
seemingly mundane circumstances.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:10.050
The SCP Foundation first became aware of SCP-3989
after a small olive orchard owner sold a strangely

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:14.600
high amount of olives that shouldn’t have
been possible when compared to his reported

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.670
number of Olea europaea olive trees.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.750
Field Agents were dispatched to question the
owner about his sudden success, but he was

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.490
resistant to questioning.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:28.520
The Agents began a covert surveillance operation
to figure what was actually going on here,

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.280
at which point they discovered a considerable
spatial anomaly.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.710
The Olive Orchard was far bigger on the inside.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.689
The property was seized by the Foundation
for containment.

00:01:38.689 --> 00:01:43.249
The owner had no real knowledge of the spatial
anomaly, it’s likely he just decided not

00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:47.689
to look a gift horse in the mouth while making
money hand over fist from the extra olives

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:48.750
he sold.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.939
The owner was given amnestics and a new life,
as the Foundation began to study this anomaly

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:57.400
which was now labeled SCP-3989.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:03.229
To this day, no researcher has been able to
figure out the origin of 3989’s anomalous

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:04.229
qualities.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:08.580
It was first given a Euclid-class designation,
and cordoned off from the public with a simple

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.830
chain link fence while Foundation investigations
were underway on inside.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:18.989
On a map, the plot of land the olive farm
should only occupy about five square acres,

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:24.099
but this plot contains an unseen portal to
a pocket dimension within its 12 meter active

00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:29.120
zone which doesn’t follow the same spatial
laws that our reality does.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:35.799
This sub-dimension, known as SCP-3989-A, is
a hotbed of fascinating anomalous activity.

00:02:35.799 --> 00:02:41.940
Upon the discovery of this hot zone, the Foundation
established the nearby Area 126 as a research

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:49.860
center and a makeshift containment facility
for any anomalous entities captured from SCP-3989-A.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:54.310
It seemed like the Foundation really had a
handle on this situation, but they were blissfully

00:02:54.310 --> 00:03:01.879
unaware of the true horrors lurking within
SCP-3989-A. But they’d soon find out…

00:03:01.879 --> 00:03:03.840
in the most horrifying way possible.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:10.120
Dr. Farik Ghazalie was assigned to head the
research into the anomalous zone within 3989,

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.650
and naturally, he began organizing fact-finding
expeditions into the heart of the affected

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:15.650
area.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:19.820
The first guinea pig to head into the hot
zone was former Foundation Agent Josiah Harrick,

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:26.051
who’d been demoted to the lowly D-Class
position of D-126-15 due to failures on a

00:03:26.051 --> 00:03:27.420
previous mission.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:31.860
With a remote link to Dr. Ghazalie, Harrick
was forced to venture into the active anomalous

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.160
zone to collect footage and samples of the
flora and fauna within.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.640
The first thing Harrick noticed on his expedition
was the strange quality of the olive trees

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.140
within the active zone.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:45.700
The bark was a stark white, and the leaves
a bloody red.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.690
Up close, Harrick could see that the trunks
and branches of the trees had undergone a

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:55.610
process known as ossification, where the material
slowly becomes bone or bone-like tissue.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:58.799
Hence the anomaly’s creepy name, The Bone
Orchard.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:03.500
These ossified trees became known as SCP-3989-1.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:08.439
Harrick also made another discovery, all over
the trees and ground were worm-like creatures

00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:15.439
that looked like long maggots that the Foundation
dubbed SCP-3989-1A.

00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:19.890
Agent Harrick then noticed that something
was off about the leaves of the ossified trees.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.250
They were beating.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:25.750
He looked closer and they appeared to be heart
tissue, filled with pumping veins.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:30.790
Dr. Ghazalie ordered Harrick to take a branch
for testing, and when he did, the tree began

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:31.840
to bleed.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.030
When he looked down, he saw that the worm-like
creatures that covered the ground were now

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.320
crawling up his legs.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:43.050
Ignoring orders from Dr. Ghazalie, Harrick
fled from the active zone in terror.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:47.380
As he left, Dr. Ghazalie caught something
in the corner of Harrick’s body-cam footage:

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:52.070
A long, white hind-limb, disappearing behind
a tree.

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:56.890
Back in our normal dimension, tests on the
samples Harrick collected yielded more upsetting

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:57.890
discoveries.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:00.550
Genetically, the trees were identical to humans.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:06.070
The trunks were human bone, and the leaves
really were made of human heart tissue.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.430
Fascinated and just a little bit horrified,
Dr. Ghazalie authorized further expeditions

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:17.470
into 3989-A. This time though, Agent Harrick
would be accompanied by another D-Class, and

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.030
both would be armed with handguns and protective
body armor.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:26.480
As it would turn out, this expedition would
be even more horrifying than the first.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.390
As the two D-Classes explored the active zone
to collect further samples, they found that

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:36.740
the worms were responsible for the ossification
of the otherwise non-anomalous olive trees.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:42.020
They consumed the wood, little by little,
and deposited human bone matter in return.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.020
Harrick and his companion also noticed that
these trees were beginning to bear fruit.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:50.400
Dr. Ghazalie ordered Harrick to collect some
of this fruit for testing, but when they attempted

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:55.300
to remove the fruit it burst, releasing more
worm-creatures.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:06:00.160
It seemed that the converted trees acted as
incubators for their egg sacs.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.020
Before the duo could return with the samples
they were able to take, the creature that’d

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:08.380
been spotted on Harrick’s body cam during
the first mission finally appeared.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:15.540
It was huge, with long, white limbs, and no
facial features except for a huge mouth.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:20.750
It grabbed Harrick’s companion and literally
ate the top half of his body in a single bite,

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.290
before dropping his legs to the ground.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:31.400
This horrifying beast, and the many others
like it, would later be designated as SCP-3989-2A.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.580
Harrick pulled out his side arm and shot the
creature several times.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.880
The creature ignored the bullets though and
charged Harrick.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.990
The feed from his bodycam cut soon after.

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:45.900
Both men were declared killed in action, and
in recognition of his sacrifice, Josiah Harrick

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:50.010
was posthumously reinstated to his old position
in the Foundation.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.860
Job well done, Agent.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:55.550
Dr. Ghazalie, meanwhile, prepared for the
next mission.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:07:00.060
This time, knowing of the clear dangers present
within The Bone Orchard, Dr. Ghazalie recruited

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.370
the help of MTF Zeta-9, aka The Mole Rats.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:09.480
Three members, referred to as Charlie Team,
were sent into the anomalous zone, once again

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.830
remotely directed by Dr. Ghazalie.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:16.170
They were equipped with experimental ultrasound
technology so that they could scan the fruit

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:24.020
of the trees within 3989-A without breaking
any and incurring the wrath of 3989-2A, which

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:27.160
seemed to act as sentries for the trees.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:31.110
Early on in their journey, they found the
body of Agent Harrick crucified against one

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:36.300
of the ossified trees, his skin covered in
mysterious symbols that were likely of a Sarkic

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.300
origin.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:41.520
While we don’t have time to fully explore
Sarkicism, that will require a video explanation

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.050
all of its own, all you need to know is that
it’s a dangerous religious cult that worships

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:53.270
flesh and disease and has close ties to similar,
dangerous anomalies like SCP - 610, also known

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.300
as the Flesh That Hates.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:59.830
People familiar with that SCP will note eerily
strange similarities to some of the things

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.410
the Mole Rats were about to encounter.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:08.550
As Charlie Team explored, they saw a huge
number of 3989-2As observing them with eyeless

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.970
faces from between the ossified trees.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.420
They pressed on, until they discovered what
seemed to be an entirely new kind of tree

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.970
within the Bone Orchard.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:25.220
SCP-3989-2 were huge trees made out of what
appears to be enlarged human spines in place

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:26.310
of a trunk.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:31.010
The smaller twigs on the tree were made from
heart and lung tissue, and the whole thing

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:35.139
was covered in what appeared to be human amniotic
sacs.

00:08:35.139 --> 00:08:39.370
Charlie Team attempted to use their ultrasound
scanners to discover the contents of these

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:46.100
sacs, but one of them exploded in the process,
releasing an entirely new variety of monster.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:53.180
From the sacs emerged the larval stage of
SCP-3989-2B, smaller humanoid monsters with

00:08:53.180 --> 00:09:00.500
no faces, no sensory organs, two pelvises.,
four legs, and an exposed spine.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:05.120
Suddenly, Charlie Team could feel a horrifying
Sarkic presence around them, which one member

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:09.950
of the team described as being like someone
grabbing her liver and giggling in her face.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:14.360
As the various monsters of the Bone Orchard
began to converge on the team, the voice of

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:19.589
the Sarkic prophet of war and the hunt, Orok,
began sounding in their ears.

00:09:19.589 --> 00:09:22.670
He was beckoning them to join him.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:27.450
While Charlie Team fled from the active zone,
Dr. Ghazalie felt increasingly drawn into

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.450
it.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:31.730
He heard the voice of Orok, and he liked what
he heard.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:37.209
Little by little, the workers of Area 126
were losing their minds, manipulated by the

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:42.200
Sarkic power of the Bone Orchard right next
to them, day after day.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:48.310
They were no longer loyal to the Foundation,
they wanted to serve their new dark masters.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.550
The fourth and final expedition was led by
Dr. Ghazalie himself.

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:57.579
He took a band of loyal followers, and one
non-believer, on a quest into the active zone

00:09:57.579 --> 00:10:02.910
to find an Orokian temple they believed was
hidden in the very heart of the Bone Orchard.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:07.980
Once they were inside, Ghazalie and his loyalists
murdered the non-believer as a sacrifice to

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.180
their new master.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:14.649
They carried on until they eventually found
what they were looking for: A giant, stone

00:10:14.649 --> 00:10:19.660
temple resembling an Aztec ziggurat, dubbed
SCP-3989-4.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:27.610
There, they also encountered a new kind of
monster, dubbed SCP-3989-3.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:31.959
These beasts were larger than the others,
and resembled ancient warriors.

00:10:31.959 --> 00:10:37.790
They had insect-like exoskeletal armor, horned
heads, additional hind and forelimbs, and

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.639
integrated bladed weapons.

00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:44.040
What Dr. Ghazalie and his companions thought
would be paradise turned out to be a kind

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:49.430
of Hell as they were led into the temple,
where temporal and spatial distortions broke

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:58.639
their mind, and the multiple, highly aggressive
instances of SCP-3989- 3, -2A, and -2B broke

00:10:58.639 --> 00:11:00.089
their bodies.

00:11:00.089 --> 00:11:02.860
The whole thing had been a horrifying trap.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:08.899
In that moment, back at Area 126, another
fleshy, horrifying tree sprouted out of the

00:11:08.899 --> 00:11:11.930
ground in the middle of the complex.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:17.540
Monsters that had once been Dr. Ghazalie and
his followers emerged from its amniotic sacs,

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:20.769
and all hell broke loose throughout the complex.

00:11:20.769 --> 00:11:25.350
Soon enough, the base was crawling with monsters
from the Bone Orchard and staff who’d become

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:29.709
brainwashed, Sarkic cultists working in service
of Orok.

00:11:29.709 --> 00:11:34.649
Humans were gathered up to be sacrificed to
the ever-growing number of anomalous trees.

00:11:34.649 --> 00:11:39.459
Things came to a head when the anomaly and
Area 126 was visited by an outside agent from

00:11:39.459 --> 00:11:44.310
the Foundation working on behalf of the Hazardous
Materials Containment Liaison.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:49.259
Biological Containment Specialist Dr. Marshall
Grant and his team arrived at the site and

00:11:49.259 --> 00:11:52.999
were horrified to see the Sarkic nightmare
that had unfolded.

00:11:52.999 --> 00:11:57.500
They quickly engaged in a firefight with the
anomalous creatures and Sarkic Devotees who’d

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:00.319
gained control over Area 126.

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:04.870
A number of Dr. Grant’s team were lost in
the process, but thankfully, they were able

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:09.019
to eventually regain control of the base and
the anomalous area.

00:12:09.019 --> 00:12:14.990
After this incident, SCP-3989 was upgraded
to Keter Class and given a huge upgrade in

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:20.529
security, including four meter high concrete
walls and a platoon sized regiment of Mobile

00:12:20.529 --> 00:12:23.059
Task Force members with heavy weaponry.

00:12:23.059 --> 00:12:30.240
The force that took over the minds of those
exposed was designated SCP-3989-V, a force

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:35.779
so powerful that those infected are given
the choice to self-terminate… or be contained

00:12:35.779 --> 00:12:36.959
forever.

00:12:36.959 --> 00:12:42.689
This may seem like a somewhat happy ending
to a grim tale, but one detail keeps Dr. Grant,

00:12:42.689 --> 00:12:48.269
and everyone at the Foundation who is forced
to deal with 3989 awake at night.

00:12:48.269 --> 00:12:53.670
According to all recent studies into the Bone
Orchard, it isn’t contained at all.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:57.629
In fact, the active zone… is getting bigger...

00:12:57.629 --> 00:13:05.059
Now go check out “SCP-4000 - Taboo” and
“SCP-5545 - Abnormality” for more strange,

00:13:05.059 --> 00:13:08.029
nightmare locations from the SCP Foundation!

